a0d0b4bdf6ba3","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/655fe85f7506862d03a5999a651a0d0b4bdf6ba3","commit_subject":"Server: each session's new TCP connections are limited, by default to 200 a second (MaxTcpConnectsPerSecond in the session options), its TUN adapter's SYNs and its TCP proxy requests on one budget, and NetScanLimit now covers the TCP connections through its TUN adapter too, where it saw only its proxy's; NetProtector, now a plain class, takes NetProtectorOptions, only the settings it needs. After Sol's review: the limits judge the mapped destination, as the TCP proxy's did; the connection rate is checked before NetScan, so a flood over it costs NetScan nothing; WindowRateLimiter's window and count change in one compare-exchange, so a window's turn can neither lose counts nor reset a later window, and a refusal writes nothing; NetScan no longer refuses a network whose cleanup leaves exactly NetScanLimit endpoints","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T21:18:37Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"6587ed6f7fc9067cecdc46fb785bcc198188586e","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/6587ed6f7fc9067cecdc46fb785bcc198188586e","commit_subject":"Server: NetProtector, WindowRateLimiter and NetScanDetector move into a NetProtection folder and namespace (VpnHood.Core.Server.NetProtection); no other change","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T21:18:33Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"8c648727f7d798d8479084dd765d25842ce59f01","github_link":"https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/commit/8c648727f7d798d8479084dd765d25842ce59f01","commit_subject":"Reshoot the SV-type and RHD figures with the OKLCH dosage ramp","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"jinja2cpp/Jinja2Cpp","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-23T21:18:30Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"31091e805b6275a683429f9ee05c9246f900be1f","github_link":"https://github.com/jinja2cpp/Jinja2Cpp/commit/310